**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests`

**How to implement.** The naming template's grammar as pure Domain: the pieces a template's text holds, and the refusal of a text that is none (001 §J 'Naming template … It names setups and experiments, and PARSES names back to match imported data'; .spec-md §5 'Setup, SetupName, slots, NamingTemplate'). The template speaks the polarimeter's words, as 001 §J's example and 001 §O's experiment matrix ('rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer') do: the source is the polarization source, S8.2's Prep slots (step 257), and the light is the light source, S8.2's Source slot; this is what makes 001's example name a setup whose Prep 1 holds `CPL1` `CPL-(…)-CPL`, as 001 §A's kit layout does. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs`: `module NamingTemplates` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `Setups.fs` (step 256), because a placeholder names a `SlotRole` (step 257): one `<Compile Include="NamingTemplates.fs" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the kit's naming template, its grammar, and the names it writes and reads (spec 0050 S8.3). It opens `Kit` and `Setups`. (2) `NamePart of string` with `.value`: one piece of text a name holds (an item's name, the note, or the literal text between placeholders). (3) `NameAlias = { label : ItemLabel; part : NamePart }`: in its placeholder, the kit item of that label is written as `part` (001 §A: the items `CPL1` and `CPL2` of a kit whose setups are named `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`). (4) `PlaceholderNeed` = `RequiredPlaceholder` | `OptionalPlaceholder`. (5) `TemplatePlaceholder` = `SlotPlaceholder of SlotRole` | `AnglePlaceholder of SlotPosition` | `NotePlaceholder`. `member this.text : string` is the placeholder's word with its number: `light` (`SourceSlotRole`), `source<k>` (`PrepSlotRole k`), `obj<k>` (`ObjectSlotRole k`), `analyzer<k>` (`AnalyzerSlotRole k`), `detector<k>` (`DetectorSlotRole k`), `phi<k>` (the angle of Obj k) and `note`. `member this.need : PlaceholderNeed` is `OptionalPlaceholder` for a slot or angle of position 2 or more and for the note, and `RequiredPlaceholder` for `light` and for the first slot of each role and its angle. A placeholder is never stored apart from the template's text, so it carries no wire tag. (6) `TemplateValue = { placeholder : TemplatePlaceholder; aliases : NameAlias list }` and `TemplatePiece` = `LiteralPiece of NamePart` | `ValuePiece of TemplateValue`. (7) `NamingTemplateError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the template's text, the placeholder or the name: `TemplateSyntaxErr` (a brace without its partner, a word or number that names no placeholder, a malformed alias, or an alias on an angle or the note), `DuplicatePlaceholderErr` (one placeholder twice, `{source}` with `{source1}` included), `AdjacentPlaceholdersErr` (two placeholders with no text between them, which no name could tell apart), `DuplicateAliasErr` (one placeholder aliasing one label twice, ignoring case, or two labels as one part), `MissingNameValueErr` (a required placeholder holds nothing, steps 269 and 271), `NameMismatchErr` (a name the template does not fit, step 269) and `UnknownNameItemErr` (a part names no kit item, step 271); `member this.describe : string` renders them `the naming template is not valid: <reason>`, `the naming template names a placeholder twice: <reason>`, `the naming template has two placeholders with nothing between them: <reason>`, `the naming template aliases an item twice: <reason>`, `the name has nothing for a placeholder it needs: <reason>`, `the name does not fit the naming template: <reason>` and `the name names no item of the kit: <reason>`. (8) `type NamingTemplate with`: `member this.pieces : Result<TemplatePiece list, NamingTemplateError>` reads the text left to right. Text outside braces is a `LiteralPiece` (a run of it is one piece, and an empty one is never made). A `{` opens a placeholder that runs to the next `}` and holds a word (`light`, `source`, `obj`, `phi`, `analyzer`, `detector` or `note`), then an optional number (ASCII digits not starting with `0`; `light` and `note` take none; no number is 1, so `{source}` is Prep 1 and `{analyzer}` is Analyzer 1), then, after a `:`, a comma-separated list of `label=part` aliases, each label and part non-empty and holding none of `{`, `}`, `:`, `=` and `,`, the label made by `ItemLabel.tryCreate` (step 213), aliases being allowed on a slot placeholder only. A `}` outside a placeholder or a `{` inside one is `TemplateSyntaxErr`. It then refuses a placeholder that appears twice, two `ValuePiece`s with no `LiteralPiece` between them, and an alias list that repeats a label (its text ignoring case) or a part. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<NamingTemplate, NamingTemplateError>` answers `NamingTemplate text` when its `pieces` answer `Ok`, and their error otherwise. The scanning is done by locals inside these members, so no module-level signature carries a primitive (ELEV003P, ELEV010P). No regular expression, cache or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs`, `module NamingTemplateTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. `the standard template is the lab's: the source, two objects at their angles, the analyzer and the note`: `NamingTemplate.standard.pieces` answers, in order, the values `SlotPlaceholder (PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))`, then `ObjectSlotRole 1`, `AnglePlaceholder 1`, `ObjectSlotRole 2`, `AnglePlaceholder 2`, `AnalyzerSlotRole 1` and `NotePlaceholder`, none with an alias, with the literals `-(`, `#`, `-`, `#`, `)-` and `-` between them; Prep 1, Obj 1, its angle and Analyzer 1 are `RequiredPlaceholder`, and Obj 2, its angle and the note `OptionalPlaceholder`. `a placeholder without a number names the first slot of its role, and each role has its word`: the pieces of `{light}/{source2}/{obj3}/{phi3}/{analyzer}/{detector2}/{note}.csv` hold, between the literals `/` and ending with `.csv`, the placeholders `SourceSlotRole`, `PrepSlotRole 2`, `ObjectSlotRole 3`, `AnglePlaceholder 3`, `AnalyzerSlotRole 1`, `DetectorSlotRole 2` and `NotePlaceholder`, whose `text`s are `light`, `source2`, `obj3`, `phi3`, `analyzer1`, `detector2` and `note`. `an alias writes a kit item under another name in its placeholder`: `{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}` holds `PrepSlotRole 1` with the aliases `CPL1` as `CPL` and `LP1` as `LP`, in that order. `a text that is no naming template is refused with its reason`: `{sauce}`, `{obj0}`, `{obj01}`, `{light1}`, `{obj1`, `obj1}`, `{ob{j1}`, `{phi1:A=B}`, `{note:A=B}`, `{source:CPL1}` and `{source:=CPL}` answer `TemplateSyntaxErr`; `{source}-{source1}` `DuplicatePlaceholderErr`; `{obj1}{phi1}` `AdjacentPlaceholdersErr`; `{source:CPL1=CPL,cpl1=C}` and `{source:A=CPL,B=CPL}` `DuplicateAliasErr`; `tryCreate` of each answers the same error, and `tryCreate` of the standard text answers `NamingTemplate.standard`. `every naming template error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it.

**Acceptance.** After the grammar lands, `NamingTemplates.fs` MUST hold `NamePart`, `NameAlias`, `PlaceholderNeed`, `TemplatePlaceholder`, `TemplateValue`, `TemplatePiece` and `NamingTemplateError`, `NamingTemplate.pieces` MUST read 001 §J's template into its values and literals and `tryCreate` MUST refuse every malformed text with its typed error; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the standard template is the lab's: the source, two objects at their angles, the analyzer and the note`, `a placeholder without a number names the first slot of its role, and each role has its word`, `an alias writes a kit item under another name in its placeholder`, `a text that is no naming template is refused with its reason` and `every naming template error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.
